<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 8 June, from 218 to 1968.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World Oceans Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Officially recognised by the United Nations in 2008, World Oceans Day highlights the ocean's critical role in sustaining life on Earth and promotes global action to protect marine ecosystems from pollution and overexploitation.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/elagabalus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elagabalus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">218 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,808 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elagabalus's legions defeat Emperor Macrinus at Antioch</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legionaries</a> backing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elagabalus">Elagabalus</a>, commanded by Gannys, defeated Emperor Macrinus and his son Diadumenian at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> when Macrinus's troops broke ranks after he fled. Macrinus was intercepted near Chalcedon and executed in Cappadocia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elagabalus">Elagabalus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/632">632 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,394 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prophet Muhammad dies in Medina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Muhammad died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, by most traditions on this day. Within a generation his successors, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>, had carried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/793">793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vikings raid the monastery of Lindisfarne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Norse raiders attacked the island monastery off Northumbria, killing monks and seizing treasure. The shock across Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> has made the raid a symbolic start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1042">1042 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">984 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward the Confessor becomes King of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-the-unready">Æthelred the Unready</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emma-of-normandy">Emma of Normandy</a>, succeeded his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harthacnut">Harthacnut</a> as king of the English. He had been raised in exile in Normandy during the Danish rule of Cnut and his sons.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1191">1191 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">835 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Richard I lands at Acre during the Third Crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a> landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> with his forces, joining the French and German armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a> already there. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> recovered Acre and much of the coast, but not <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1191">1191 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">835 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard the Lionheart arrives at the siege of Acre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> joined the crusaders besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>, which surrendered five weeks later. He went on to win at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a> but never retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Jackson dies at the Hermitage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The seventh US president died at his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> plantation aged 78. Victor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> and champion of the 'common man', he also drove the forced removal of Native Americans.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1949">1949 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">77 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Orwell's Nineteen Eighty-Four is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secker and Warburg published George Orwell's novel of a totalitarian surveillance state. Terms such as 'Big Brother' and 'doublethink' passed into everyday language.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Earl Ray is arrested at Heathrow</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> King's killer was caught at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Heathrow travelling on a false Canadian passport. He pleaded guilty in 1969 and was sentenced to 99 years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
